//@version=6
// The only shape that makes every-update cadence show something a bar-close run
// cannot: a RESTING order whose fill depends on how far the bar has developed.
//
//   bun examples/pinelive/every-update-runner.ts \
//     --strategy examples/pinelive/intrabar-stop-entry.pine --revisions 6
//
// Why the market-order strategies show nothing intrabar: piner's fill pass runs at
// the START of every tick (step 2 of the tick order), and a market order fills
// there regardless of the developing bar's range. So every tick of one chart bar
// reports the same position_size, and the forming evaluations are duplicates.
//
// A stop entry is different. It fills only once the developing bar's range reaches
// the level, so early revisions of a bar report flat and later revisions report the
// filled position. Because each tick begins by rolling broker state back to the
// last committed bar, that transition is re-derived per revision — which is exactly
// the "a forming target can appear and then vanish" behavior the cadence exists for.
//
// Both flags are on here, which is the combination worth understanding. They do not
// conflict: process_orders_on_close fills MARKET orders created during the bar at
// the close, while limit/stop orders and exit brackets are only checked against the
// close price. So a resting order still fills intrabar in the step-2 pass. One run
// of this strategy shows both mechanisms:
//
//   bar 1706050800  rev 1-2 flat, rev 3 -> 0.125   resting stop fills MID-BAR
//   bar 1705878000  rev 1-5 at 0.121, final 0.000  market exit defers to the CLOSE
//
// Under mirrored execution none of it would reach a broker: every forming decision
// is journaled as skipped with reason "mirrorOn=bar-close". The intrabar path is an
// observability surface, not an execution one.
strategy("Intrabar stop entry",
     overlay = true,
     initial_capital = 10000,
     default_qty_type = strategy.percent_of_equity,
     default_qty_value = 50,
     calc_on_every_tick = true,
     process_orders_on_close = true)

breakoutLength = input.int(20, "breakout", minval = 2)
exitLength = input.int(10, "exit", minval = 2)

// The level comes from COMPLETED bars only, so the developing bar cannot move it.
level = ta.highest(high, breakoutLength)[1]
exitLine = ta.sma(close, exitLength)

// Rest a stop entry above the prior range. It fills mid-bar, when the developing
// high reaches the level — not at the bar's open.
if strategy.position_size == 0 and not na(level)
    strategy.entry("long", strategy.long, stop = level)

if strategy.position_size > 0 and close < exitLine
    strategy.close("long")

plot(level, "breakout level", color = color.purple)
plot(exitLine, "exit", color = color.orange)
